1
00:00:03,068 --> 00:00:05,016
Mila rubs a balloon on her head.

2
00:00:05,147 --> 00:00:06,170
And when she lifts it…

3
00:00:06,220 --> 00:00:07,842
her hair rises with it!

4
00:00:08,878 --> 00:00:10,731
As if it were pulled by the balloon.

5
00:00:10,846 --> 00:00:11,517
Why?

6
00:00:12,871 --> 00:00:15,805
Noah has an idea: the balloon is a magnet!

7
00:00:15,910 --> 00:00:17,484
He tries a real magnet.

8
00:00:17,577 --> 00:00:18,746
Nothing moves.

9
00:00:18,839 --> 00:00:19,837
That's not it.

10
00:00:20,508 --> 00:00:21,899
Discovery mission!

11
00:00:25,518 --> 00:00:26,497
Mini mode!

12
00:00:26,612 --> 00:00:28,945
Everything is made of tiny pieces.

13
00:00:29,047 --> 00:00:32,708
Some carry a tiny charge: pluses, and minuses.

14
00:00:33,318 --> 00:00:34,219
When you rub,

15
00:00:34,269 --> 00:00:36,680
little minuses jump from the hair to the balloon.

16
00:00:36,834 --> 00:00:38,763
The hair keeps lots of pluses.

17
00:00:38,891 --> 00:00:40,899
The balloon fills up with minuses.

18
00:00:41,532 --> 00:00:44,458
And here's the rule: like charges push apart.

19
00:00:44,575 --> 00:00:47,162
Each hair is plus, its neighbor too…

20
00:00:47,279 --> 00:00:49,553
so they spread out, and stand up!

21
00:00:50,475 --> 00:00:52,612
And opposite charges pull together.

22
00:00:52,737 --> 00:00:54,075
The balloon full of minuses

23
00:00:54,125 --> 00:00:55,862
pulls the hair full of pluses.

24
00:00:56,474 --> 00:00:58,865
That's also why a rubbed balloon sticks to the wall:

25
00:00:59,098 --> 00:01:01,551
it pulls the pluses of the wall, right next to it.

26
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:05,883
Rubbing moves tiny charges: like ones push apart,

27
00:01:05,933 --> 00:01:07,587
opposite ones pull together.

28
00:01:08,345 --> 00:01:10,912
With an adult: rub a balloon on your hair,

29
00:01:10,962 --> 00:01:13,191
then bring it close to little bits of paper.

30
00:01:13,319 --> 00:01:14,624
They jump onto it!

31
00:01:15,342 --> 00:01:16,161
And where does the puddle

32
00:01:16,211 --> 00:01:18,078
water go when it disappears?

33
00:01:18,222 --> 00:01:19,586
The answer tomorrow.
